<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">K. J. Ståhlberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1865">1865</a>–<a href="/years/1952">1952</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Kaarlo Juho Ståhlberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaarlo Juho Ståhlberg was a Finnish lawyer and the first president of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>, serving from 1919 to 1925. As the main author of the republican constitution of 1919, he worked to heal the divisions of the civil war, pardoning many imprisoned Reds. In 1930 he was kidnapped by activists of the far-right <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lapua-movement">Lapua Movement</a>, an episode that discredited it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/k-j-stahlberg.jpg" alt="K. J. Ståhlberg" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaarlo_Juho_St%C3%A5hlberg_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A German prince, Frederick Charles of Hesse, was elected king in October 1918 but renounced the throne after Germany’s defeat, and the constitution of July 1919 made Finland a republic with <b>K. J. Ståhlberg</b> as its first president.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-finland">Republic of Finland · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Suomussalmi, in what is now <a href="/countries/finland">Finland</a>. Died in Helsinki, in what is now <a href="/countries/finland">Finland</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=64.89,28.91&amp;year=1921" aria-label="Suomussalmi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5125 38 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of K. J. Ståhlberg"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5575 308h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5575 308h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=64.89,28.91&amp;year=1921">What was here in 1921? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
